==English==

===Etymology 1===
A compromise between English ''CUT'' (“Coordinated Universal Time”) and French ''TUC'' (“{{lang|fr|Temps Universel Coordonné}}”), unofficially giving “Universal Time Coordinated” and “{{lang|fr|Universel Temps Coordonné}}”.

